      "writtenOn": "2020-10-30T15:34:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t appear that zephyr has a way to initialize an array of mutexes (I\u0027ll be super happy if you can find an example that proves me wrong on this but I haven\u0027t been able to find anything).\n\nThe only thing I\u0027ve been able to think of (which I really didn\u0027t like but might be worth seeing if we can upstream) is a macro to do this by: declaring N static mutexes via K_MUTEX_DEFINE, then declaring the array of static mutex_t *mutex_list[] which will point to those. This didn\u0027t seem worth it (yet).",
      "parentUuid": "b62f97e6_8960fc31",
